1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,343
Chapter twenty-one — the
experts, and the report.

2
00:00:04,403 --> 00:00:11,849
The system side has fourteen
experts. This side has its own.

3
00:00:11,909 --> 00:00:21,354
Perry the process analyst. Charlie on
change management. Dana on agile delivery.

4
00:00:21,414 --> 00:00:30,155
Ivy on incidents. Olivia on
onboarding. Priya on procurement.

5
00:00:30,215 --> 00:00:39,660
Each one reads the part of the model it
knows, with your actual numbers in it.

6
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:43,800
Analyze puts the whole
organization in front of them.

7
00:00:43,860 --> 00:01:13,385
Span of control, coordination load,
bus factor, cost — read together.

8
00:01:13,445 --> 00:01:24,831
And it comes back as findings
against your structure.

9
00:01:24,891 --> 00:01:31,901
Then the report is what leaves the building.

10
00:01:31,961 --> 00:01:40,405
Overview and capacity, the org chart,
roles and cost, coordination load,

11
00:01:40,465 --> 00:01:49,910
structure and bus factor, the step
playbooks, and an AI analysis.

12
00:01:49,970 --> 00:02:00,122
Out as PDF, Word, PowerPoint, Markdown or SVG.

13
00:02:00,182 --> 00:02:04,725
The system side proves the architecture.

14
00:02:04,785 --> 00:02:10,387
This side proves the
organization that has to run it.
